{"answers":[{"boundary":"The prime-index and prime-gap dyadic series are irrational together. The equivalence supplies neither statement; the irrationality of each stays open.","category":"restatement","certificate":"ErdosProblems.ArgumentGraph.RelationCertificates.prime_gap_view","certificate_source":"lean/ErdosProblems/ArgumentGraph/Results/RelationCertificates.lean:43","certificate_source_sha256":"7a5dc7118263b162357dc36c1a6646227ab5f754598336f37030a6f64c252c2f","family_id":"erdos_251","independent_result_count":"not_inferred","left":"Irrational (∑' n : ℕ, ErdosProblems.Erdos251.primeDyadicTerm n)","novelty":"not_inferred","relation":"equivalent","right":"Irrational (∑' n : ℕ, ErdosProblems.Erdos251.primeGapDyadicTerm n)","row_id":"prime_gap_view","row_sha256":"77e9d15e8aa15c7d76f4bf6c551c1779a30ba4771cc5e2da29b89ffcee38121d","scope":"fun _ : Unit => True","task_id":"relation_01"},{"boundary":"On 0 < b < a the power condition b ^ zudilinMu < a and the contour region agree. The guards 0 < b and b < a belong to the context; outside them no relation is recorded.","category":"restatement","certificate":"ErdosProblems.ArgumentGraph.RelationCertificates.contour_view","certificate_source":"lean/ErdosProblems/ArgumentGraph/Results/RelationCertificates.lean:58","certificate_source_sha256":"7a5dc7118263b162357dc36c1a6646227ab5f754598336f37030a6f64c252c2f","family_id":"erdos_1049","independent_result_count":"not_inferred","left":"(ab.2 : ℝ) ^ zudilinMu < (ab.1 : ℝ)","novelty":"not_inferred","relation":"equivalent","right":"ZudilinContourRegion ab.1 ab.2","row_id":"contour_view","row_sha256":"d4eda7adbec6e7caed2a9f4d671acc00657241054e666a85a9081ad6b3438ee2","scope":"fun ab : ℕ × ℕ => 0 < ab.2 ∧ ab.2 < ab.1","task_id":"relation_02"},{"boundary":"The square-root escape as the paper states it and the square escape are one statement. Neither is supplied by this equivalence.","category":"restatement","certificate":"ErdosProblems.ArgumentGraph.RelationCertificates.square_view","ce